    "source_text": "Following general procedure F using 2,2,2‐trifluoro‐N‐(3‐(2‐(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)propyl)acetamide (74.8 mg, 0.25 mmol), B2pin2 (127 mg, 0.50 mmol), [Ir(COD)OMe]2 (2.5 mg, 0.00375 mmol) and dtbpy (2.0 mg, 0.0075 mmol) in THF (1.25 mL). The reaction was stirred at 50 °C for 20 hours before cooling and the solvents removed. Analysis of crude 1 H NMR using internal standard 1,2‐dimethoxyethane showed 0.8:1 meta:para borylation in 96% yield. The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography (Pet. Ether (40‐60):EtOAc (19:1) to give the title compound (as a 1.2:1 mixture of meta:para ratio, as determined by 1 H NMR) as a colourless oil (89.0 mg, 0.21 mmol, 84%). By subtracting the resonances for the meta isomer, the NMR data of the para isomer can be assigned as follows:",
    "text_sha256": "46463869a2c48fee8000dee1e0284bc858a8c952e143402948b55f5dc82a1918",
